    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. The three test files are `AcceptanceBase` (abstract), `AuditLogCapture` (a helper), and `AcceptanceTest` (the one runnable test), and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that a created owner's response include a `displayName` formatted as `LastName, FirstName`. I made two small, cohesive changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `displayName` string property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field (input `OwnerFields` is untouched).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a single `@Mapping` expression on the existing `toOwnerDto` method:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   ```\n\nThis keeps structural impact minimal: no new logic added to the large `Owner` domain class, no new method with high surrounding complexity \u2014 just one annotation on an existing mapper method (CC 1, tiny WMC context) plus a schema declaration. The reverse `toOwner` mapping treats `displayName` as an ignored unmapped source (read-only), so nothing else changed.",
